			"notes": "TikTok in Minecraft: a phone-style panel in the corner of your screen while you play, with hotkeys to skip videos.\n\n## Download\n\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | File |\n|---|---|\n| 26.1.x | `tiktokmc-1.0.0+mc26.1.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `tiktokmc-1.0.0+mc26.2.jar` |\n| 26.3 | `tiktokmc-1.0.0+mc26.3.jar` |\n\n## Install\n\n1. Install [Fabric Loader](https://fabricmc.net/use/) for your Minecraft version.\n2. Put [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) and the jar above in `.minecraft/mods`.\n3. Have Microsoft Edge (built into Windows 10/11) or Google Chrome installed. The mod plays TikTok through a hidden copy of it, so video and sound work.\n\n## Controls\n\n| Key | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `Y` | Show/hide the TikTok panel |\n| `→` / `←` | Next / previous video |\n| `U` | Full-size TikTok with mouse and keyboard, plus **Log in** and **Reset TikTok data** buttons |\n| `M` | Mute/unmute |\n\nKeys can be changed under Options → Controls → Key Binds → TikTok.\n\n## Logging in\n\nPress `U` and click **Log in (opens window)**. Sign in in the normal Edge/Chrome window that opens, then close it. TikTok blocks logins from hidden browsers, so this is the way to sign in.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Tested in game on Minecraft 26.3. The 26.1 and 26.2 builds compile against their versions but haven't been run in game yet.\n- Client-side only; not affiliated with TikTok or Mojang."
		}
